WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.432
Gel nails lifting after just a few days? Your everyday habits may be the reason!

2
00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:09.552
Here are the five most common habits, and how to fix them.

3
00:00:09.552 --> 00:00:13.446
First: picking at the gel edges as soon as they lift a little.

4
00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:18.874
The more you pick, the more it opens, and you peel off the surface of your own nail too.

5
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:24.095
Second: opening cans, peeling labels and prying lids with your nails.

6
00:00:24.095 --> 00:00:28.834
All the leverage lands on the edge of the nail, so the gel cracks and lifts.

7
00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:33.513
Third: long sessions of washing up or laundry without gloves.

8
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:38.622
Water and detergents make the gel swell, and the edges slowly lift.

9
00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:42.769
Fourth: a sauna or a hot bath on the very first day.

10
00:00:42.769 --> 00:00:48.271
Heat and moisture make your natural nail swell, so the gel comes away more easily.

11
00:00:48.271 --> 00:00:51.811
Fifth: waiting more than four weeks for a refill.

12
00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:57.616
The nail grows, the gel moves towards the tip, and the nail breaks and lifts more easily.

13
00:00:57.616 --> 00:01:05.379
In short: don't pick, don't use your nails as tools, wear gloves, skip the sauna on day one, and refill on time.

14
00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:09.742
